Implemented Vercel Web Analytics for the Cauchy website project.

## Summary
Successfully installed and configured Vercel Web Analytics following the official Vercel documentation (https://vercel.com/docs/analytics/quickstart).

## Changes Made

### 1. Package Installation
- Installed `@vercel/analytics` version 2.0.1
- Updated package.json to include the new dependency
- Updated package-lock.json with the new package and its dependencies

### 2. Analytics Integration
Modified `src/app/layout.tsx`:
- Added import statement: `import { Analytics } from "@vercel/analytics/next"`
- Added `<Analytics />` component to the root layout's body, placed after the Footer component

### 3. Framework-Specific Implementation
This project uses Next.js 16.2.7 with the App Router pattern, so I followed the Next.js App Router instructions from the official documentation:
- Imported the Analytics component from `@vercel/analytics/next`
- Placed the component inside the `<body>` tag of the root layout
- The component will automatically track page views and web vitals

## Verification Steps Completed
✅ Build completed successfully (npm run build)
✅ No new TypeScript errors introduced
✅ Code follows existing project structure and patterns
✅ Analytics component properly integrated into the root layout

## Next Steps
To enable analytics data collection:
1. Enable Web Analytics in the Vercel dashboard for this project
2. Deploy the changes to Vercel
3. Analytics data will appear in the dashboard after deployment and user visits

## Technical Notes
- The Analytics component is placed at the end of the body to avoid blocking page render
- Used npm for package installation as bun was not available in the environment
- The existing linter warnings in logo-ideas/page.tsx are unrelated to this change
- All changes preserve the existing code structure and styling
